  "full_text": "So the people I encounter, I'll be talking with them for a while, and then it'll become obvious they're with the doctors, right? It's like, oh, you're with the doctors, aren't you? So you're like an agent that's with the doctors. So like I said, oh, so I saw this guy a little earlier. I said, hey, doctor. So basically that was one of the guys with the doctors, right? So anyway. So they'll do that shit. They come up to you. The psychologists, they got actors and shit. It's total actors. And they'll try and play games with your head. And they always let slip that they're with the doctors, you know. Basically... Pretty much everybody that I encounter is probably with the doctors. I probably don't even, you know, you probably don't really have that much normal interaction with people. But when you're being under therapy of a doctor, you're going to be getting all kinds of encounters with their doctor secret agents. So pretty much everyone on the street that encounters me is probably one of the doctor's agents. That's probably how it works. Because the chances of meeting an actual normal person is probably slim. I don't know. You really don't interact as much as you would think.",
